# ROX AI — backend Docker build context exclusions
#
# Keeps the build context small (faster `docker build`) and, more
# importantly, keeps real secrets and host-specific state OUT of the
# image entirely — .env is never copied in; real values are injected
# at `docker run`/compose time via --env-file/env_vars, never baked in.

# Dependencies — installed fresh inside the image by `npm install
# --omit=dev` (see Dockerfile); a host node_modules would just be dead
# weight, and could bake in a platform-mismatched native binary if the
# image is built on a different OS/arch than it was installed on.
node_modules

# Secrets — NEVER let a real .env reach the build context. .env.example
# is intentionally not excluded (it has no real values, and is useful
# reference inside the image/repo checkout).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host-local state that has no place in an image (logs/backups
# themselves live one level up at the repo root — outside this build
# context already — so they're excluded from ever being COPY'd purely
# by not being inside backend/ at all; this just covers stray *.log
# files that might exist directly under backend/)
*.log

# Version control / editor / OS cruft
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Tests aren't needed at runtime in the image — they still run in CI /
# on the host via `npm run test:unit`, just not shipped in the image.
test-*.js

# Docker's own files (irrelevant to include in their own build context)
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.worker
.dockerignore
